1. Scope and definitions

"Application" means original Meshable Ops code, documentation, deployment tools,
original bundled plugins and the owner's imported WeasyCanvas source supplied
under this notice, including modified, renamed, rebranded, source and compiled
versions. Identified third-party material retains its separate terms.

"Licensor" means Graham Hill as original creator and any lawful successor holding
the relevant rights. A "Licensing Maintainer" is a current maintainer expressly
appointed in writing by the Licensor to grant commercial permissions within that
appointment's scope. Fork maintainers, repository administrators, commit access
and contributor status alone do not confer licensing authority.

"Internal Use" means conducting a person's or organization's own operations,
including commercial operations and private modifications. Staff, contractors
acting solely on its behalf and customers/suppliers accessing its business
records/processes may participate. It excludes selling/licensing the Application
and providing its functionality as a hosted software product to third parties.

"Commercial Offering" means selling, licensing, renting, sublicensing for payment,
commercially distributing or otherwise monetizing copies of the Application,
or offering its functionality as a commercial hosted, managed, SaaS or similar
service to third parties. It includes direct, bundled, advertising-supported and
indirect commercial consideration, whether modified or unmodified. Ordinary
revenue from a business's own goods/services does not make its Internal Use a
Commercial Offering merely because the Application supports those operations.

"Plugin" means a separately identifiable extension installed through the plugin
interfaces. Repackaging or moving core Application functionality into an extension
does not qualify it for the exception in section 4.

"Complete Source" means the preferred form for modifying covered code, including
modifications and scripts/material needed to build, install and run it, excluding
credentials, business records and independent system components. A link to an
unrelated or outdated source tree is insufficient.

