Subject to this license, the Licensor grants a worldwide, nonexclusive,
royalty-free copyright license to inspect, run, copy and modify the Application
for Internal Use, evaluation, education and noncommercial purposes; to develop
Plugins; and to distribute or provide remote access for noncommercial purposes
under section 3. Paid installation, training, consulting, customization and
maintenance on systems owned or controlled by the customer are permitted unless
they include an unauthorized Commercial Offering. No copyright ownership or
trademark rights are transferred.

You may not make a Commercial Offering of the Application without separate
written commercial permission from the Licensor or a Licensing Maintainer acting
within their authority. This applies to forks, derivatives and unmodified copies.
Preserving notices, providing source, donating or contributing upstream does not
itself grant commercial permission. A written agreement may specify fees,
development/maintenance contributions, covered versions and other terms.

3. Source, notices and downstream terms

When distributing covered code, include this license and applicable copyright,
attribution and third-party notices; identify material modifications; and provide
its Complete Source to recipients at no additional charge. License your covered
modifications under these same community terms. Do not withdraw these community
permissions or purport to grant commercial Application rights you do not own.

If you operate a modified covered version over a network, prominently offer its
users the Complete Source of that version at no additional charge. The offer may
require the deployment's normal account access. This requirement does not permit
an otherwise prohibited Commercial Offering. Internal modifications need not be
published to the general public solely because of Internal Use, but this network
source requirement still applies to users of a modified deployment.

Ordinary business records, generated documents, uploaded files, personal data
and secrets do not become covered code merely because the Application processes
them. Do not include private data or credentials in source offers.

4. Paid community plugins and integration components

Plugin authors may charge for copies, paywalled access, subscriptions, hosting,
support and services for their separately identifiable Plugins and retain the
proceeds without an automatic royalty/revenue share to the Licensor. This express
exception applies to the Plugin itself. It does not permit selling, bundling for
a commercial charge or commercially hosting the Application, or a substitute
hosted offering of its core functionality, as a device to evade section 2.

Application-derived code and covered Plugin extensions inherit this license,
including this exception and section 3's source/notice conditions. Authors retain
ownership of their original Plugin code. A paywall cannot withdraw recipients'
permitted rights or charge extra for required source. Publishing or selling an
independent Plugin does not accept a CLA or grant the Licensor relicensing rights
over that Plugin. An identified contribution expressly accepted under the CLA
is governed by that agreement to its stated extent.

Independently authored, separable external-service clients/adapters may retain
another license where it permits the actual combination and distribution.
Preserve its notices, source and other requirements. Independent remote services
retain their own terms. An API, ZIP, language or process boundary alone does not
exempt Application-derived code or eliminate third-party obligations.

